dot_emacs Repository Version History
====================================

v26.08 (Release Date: TBD)
--------------------------
- Remove the obsolete navi2ch and Riece configuration, along with their key
  bindings, and keep the optional italk load in autoloads.el.
- Remove jade-mode, keeping the Stylus support of sws-mode.el as a
  standalone third-party file, with its stale jade-mode load-path and
  byte-compile entries removed.
- Remove zencoding-mode, including the copy bundled inside nXhtml, along
  with its mode hooks and key bindings, while keeping nXhtml itself.
- Remove web-mode, flymake-cursor and anything-complete.
- Remove the bundled ESS and its compatibility bridge; ESS is now an
  external user-managed dependency when R or S support is needed.
- Remove the legacy Meadow support, including dot_emacs_on_meadow, and the
  pre-Emacs-23 fallbacks such as wb-line-number, while retaining GNU Emacs
  23.4 as the minimum supported version.
- Remove the unused auto-complete-config.el helper library and the
  auto-complete-pkg.el metadata file.
- Replace the bundled Helm path for Emacs 24 through 26 with Anything on
  every supported Emacs version, and move its configuration into
  anything-settings.el.
- Replace jaspace with the standard whitespace mode, enabled globally from
  whitespace-settings.el, and remove the bundled jaspace.el, whose display
  table showed an ASCII @ as a box.
- Replace count-lines-region, removed in Emacs 29, with count-lines in
  sws-mode.el, so indenting a region in sws-mode works again.
- Replace zlc with the built-in minibuffer-visible-completions navigation
  on GNU Emacs 30+, while GNU Emacs 23.4 through 29.x retain the
  historical zlc path.
- Add savehist persistence for the minibuffer history and the kill ring
  with an explicit 300-second autosave interval, while savekill keeps
  saving the kill ring immediately on every update.
- Add the Apple Silicon Homebrew directory /opt/homebrew/bin to exec-path
  and PATH when it exists.
- Add .gitattributes, marking the Markdown documents for diff and the
  vendored third-party README files as vendored.
- Add a README Directory Structure section describing each main directory.
- Expand doc/GUIDELINES with the deliberate retirement of a legacy
  component, the scope of byte compilation, the document file naming and
  attribute recommendations, the reach of a compatibility bridge and when a
  bundled file may be edited instead, the scope and history of a pull
  request, the width a version history entry keeps, and when an executable
  script's own version is updated.
- Change byte compilation to a selective policy: init.el, autoloads.el,
  configs.el, lang-mode.el, screen.el, diminish-settings.el and
  anything-settings.el are loaded from source, and the installer and the
  auto-async-byte-compile exclusion list agree on them.
- Change the installer byte compilation to a per-file best effort that
  reports each failed file, counts the results and continues instead of
  aborting the installation.
- Stop the installer when its existing target cannot be removed, so stale
  files are not mixed with the new configuration.
- Let find-file open nonexistent paths as editable new files instead of
  routing them through view-mode.
- Silence the native compilation warning pop-up in init.el, keeping the
  entries in the *Warnings* buffer.
- Treat the Cocoa ns window system like mac in global-set-key.el, so C-h is
  no longer translated to DEL there.
- Use the historical /opt/python/current environment only when its
  directory and interpreter exist, and bind C-c p to python-pep8 only
  when that command is available.
- Move the bundled cl-lib.el forward-compatibility copy into its own
  directory and add it to load-path only on GNU Emacs 23.4 through 24.2,
  so GNU Emacs 24.3+ uses its built-in cl-lib instead of shadowing it.
- Pass the bundled cl-lib directory to the dired-async child process on GNU
  Emacs 23.4 through 24.2, where the emacs -Q child cannot require cl-lib
  otherwise, and add nothing there on GNU Emacs 24.3+.
- Fix the with-eval-after-load fallback so deferred Anything key bindings
  run correctly on GNU Emacs 23.4 through 24.3.
- Fix the asynchronous byte compilation status so that any nonzero exit
  status is reported as an error, through a project-owned replacement for
  aabc/status which recognized only status 1.
- Require core-compat-bridge when compiling auto-save-buffers-enhanced.el,
  so its toggle-read-only call no longer warns.
- Declare the conditionally defined and optional functions of the bundled
  browse-kill-ring.el, auto-save-buffers-enhanced.el and
  minibuf-isearch.el, so the compiler no longer reports them as unknown.
- Absorb the obsolete cl aliases in cl-compat-bridge.el, so the bundled
  files that still load cl stop reporting every call.
- Fix cl-compat-bridge.el so GNU Emacs 24.3+ also requires the obsolete
  cl package when cl-lib lacks lexical-let and lexical-let*, restoring
  their historical closure semantics for bundled deferred, concurrent
  and Anything callbacks that capture lexical bindings for later use.
- Clarify the license exclusions for bundled third-party software and
  project files containing third-party-derived code.
- Update the README overview and default behavior sections to match the
  bundled software that remains.
- Reword the Policy header line of the project-owned files to preserve
  supported behavior, and give it the terminating period of the
  doc/GUIDELINES example.
- Wrap the lines of this file at 75 columns.
- Record the shared version history description guidelines at the end of
  this file.

v26.07 (2026-07-31)
-------------------
- Resolve the installer script directory before changing the working
  directory, so relative invocations work.
- Byte-compile with the elisp load path, so bundled files requiring the
  compatibility bridges are compiled.
- Allow nosudo installs and uninstalls to run when the sudo command is
  unavailable.
- Add -n and --no-sudo aliases for the installer and uninstaller.
- Replace awk {n,} interval expression in usage() with a portable
  equivalent for mawk compatibility.
- Build the bundled helm only on Emacs 24 through 26, where it is actually
  loaded, since its Makefile fails on newer Emacs.
- Drop the unreachable adaptive history cleanup from the uninstaller.
- Declare my-load-path with defvar in init.el before assigning it.
- Fix the dired-async loader so dired-async-mode is enabled at startup.
- Simplify the redundant timidity autoload wrapper in autoloads.el.
- Fix the recentf-ext-settings.el load typo and clean up two obsolete
  autoload entries.
- Remove the unused auto-save-buffers block from autoloads.el, which could
  double up with auto-save-buffers-enhanced.
- Remove the obsolete default-major-mode setting, which no longer affects
  the major mode of new buffers.
- Add a quiet argument to load-p and use it for the optional site-lisp
  loader, which reported a failure on every startup.
- Stay quiet about the italk, mic-paren, and develock loaders, which are
  not bundled and failed on every startup.
- Disable the blinking cursor explicitly, since a nil argument now enables
  the mode instead of toggling it.
- Replace the obsolete find-file-hooks alias with find-file-hook in
  configs.el.
- Set temporary-file-directory to /dev/shm only on GNU/Linux, since
  platforms such as macOS have no such directory.
- Stop redefining the built-in previous-buffer, and bind M-n to a new
  forward-buffer command instead.
- Turn off hl-line in toggle-view-mode by calling hl-line-mode instead of
  assigning to its variable.
- Disable the malformed view-mode "." key entry, which signalled a commandp
  error instead of running a command.
- Require dired in dired-settings.el, which relied on another library to
  load dired-mode-map first.
- Apply the navi2ch proxy user and password only when the proxy is enabled.
- Fix with-suppressed-message so message-log-max is bound at run time
  instead of macro expansion time.
- Require cl-compat-bridge instead of the obsolete cl package in
  multi-term-settings.el.
- Bridge the legacy CL names cl-lib provides only with a cl- prefix, such
  as first, block, return, getf and subseq, which broke Rinari loading and
  C-x b on Emacs 30.
- Add a lexical-let* shim next to the existing lexical-let one, which
  anything-config.el and other bundled files still use.
- Give dolist and dotimes an implicit nil block, so legacy return calls
  keep working without the obsolete cl package.
- Guard set-face-bold-p calls in faces.el with fboundp to avoid breaking
  font-lock-mode-hook if the obsolete function is removed.
- Guard screen.el against an unset TERM environment variable to avoid a
  string-match error on startup.
- Drop the redundant .el suffix from the markdown-mode autoload-p call in
  lang-mode.el for consistency.
- Remove the bundled shadow.el and its settings, which collided with the
  built-in shadow.el and broke find-file.
- Remove the unused new-file-p.el and the bundled foreign-regexp.el, which
  are no longer loaded.
- Remove web-mode-settings.el, whose indentation settings used web-mode 7
  variable names that web-mode 8 ignores.
- Require scala-mode-auto optionally in lang-mode.el, since a missing
  scala-mode aborted the rest of the startup.
- Keep the built-in gensym in cl-compat-bridge.el instead of aliasing it to
  cl-gensym.
- Stop calling viewer-stay-in-setup twice in view-mode-key.el, and provide
  the feature under the file name.
- Add to python-mode-hook and gtags-mode-hook instead of replacing them, so
  other settings survive.
- Replace quoted lambdas in hooks and timers with plain ones, which lexical
  binding turns into closures.
- Compare emacs-major-version against plain numbers instead of quoted ones.
- Correct the toggle-read-only comment in core-compat-bridge.el, which
  described the shim as being for old Emacs.

